            <ArticleTitle>Assessment and management of a patient with a renal transplant.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>656-62</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Renal transplant recipients admitted on the medical take can be challenging for the clinician. Immunosuppressant medications, reduced renal functional reserve, increased vascular risk, and propensity to uncommon infections and malignancies all contribute to make management more complex than in other patients. This article reviews salient points in the management of such patients by the non-specialist.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
